# 10-Database-Audit-Security-Monitoring - Requirements and Objectives

## Scenario Objectives:
1. Installation and configuration of PostgreSQL 16 and the pgaudit extension on Ubuntu.
2. Deployment of Wazuh Manager and Wazuh Agent via Docker/Native packages.
3. Configuration of the Wazuh Agent to monitor PostgreSQL text audit logs (`stderr`).
4. Preparation of custom Wazuh detection rules (detecting DDL queries - level 10, and SELECT queries - level 6).
5. Implementation of the Active Response mechanism (automatic blocking of attacking IPs from Kali Linux using iptables while preserving Wazuh agent connectivity).
6. Execution of attack and query simulations from Kali Linux and validation in Wazuh Dashboard.
